# @name: aws | Create EC2 Instance
# @description: Launches a new EC2 instance with specified parameters Group: AWS EC2 Commands. Template: replace placeholders before running. {ami_id} = The ID of the Amazon Machine Image (e.g., ami-1234567890abcdef0) | {instance_type} = The type of instance (e.g., t2.micro) [default "t2.micro"] | {key_name} = The name of the key pair | {security_group_id} = The ID of the security group | {subnet_id} = The ID of the subnet
aws ec2 run-instances --image-id {ami_id} --instance-type {instance_type} --key-name {key_name} --security-group-ids {security_group_id} --subnet-id {subnet_id}